/**
 * Infrastructure layer (spec-01 &sect;2.1) &mdash; persistence for the CQRS read models, agent traces and briefings, the Kafka Streams topology, and the LLM integration (Week 9: FR14, and from 4 October 2026 FR15). <p>The service's ports are declared in {@code application} (spec-01 &sect;2.3, ADR 0002 Decision 2, ADR 0004) and the adapters here implement them. The {@code domain} package added by ADR 0006 on 4 October 2026 holds the risk policy and the value it produces and declares no port; until that date this note read "there is no {@code domain} package in this service to depend inward on". The service is a Conformist consumer (spec-01 &sect;1.5) that accepts the upstream event models from the {@code contracts} module without negotiation. <p>As of Week 7 this package holds FR12 and FR13 in one topology: the windowed sell-through aggregate over {@code item-sold}, the {@code KTable} of velocity baselines, the {@code KTable} of live batch state folded from {@code batch-received} and {@code stock-level-changed}, the stream-table join between them, and the Interactive Query adapters that serve {@code GET /api/insight/velocity/&#123;sku&#125;} and {@code GET /api/insight/risks} from the resulting state stores. <p>Note what is NOT here. The risk arithmetic and its threshold live in {@code domain}'s {@code RiskAssessmentPolicy} (in {@code application} until ADR 0006), not in the topology, because the topology and the read side must reach the same verdict &mdash; otherwise a batch could be alarmed by one and reported safe by the other. The topology decides <i>when</i> to assess; the policy decides <i>what the answer is</i>. <p>Note {@code OccurredAtTimestampExtractor}. Kafka Streams would otherwise window on the broker record timestamp, and spec-01 &sect;2.6 requires producer-assigned {@code occurredAt} and forbids relying on ingestion time. It is one line of configuration per binding and the correctness of every windowed number depends on it.
 */
